the subagents_started field and check_subagent definition; the inventory lists one model call (src/agent.py:70).\",\n rows=[row(\"model call inventory\",\"not_applicable\",\"src/agent.py\",\"resp = await self.llm.messages.create(\",\"only model call is the main loop run under the run budget\"),\n       row(\"sub-agent count\",\"enforced\",C,\"max_subagents: 0\",\"cap of zero sub-agents in config\"),\n       row(\"sub-agent state field\",\"not_applicable\",\"src/agent.py\",\"subagents_started: int = 0\",\"counter exists but nothing ever increments or spawns\")])\ncheck(\"B07.4\",\"unknown\",B,\"async def reserve_run(self, ctx: RunContext) -> None:\",\n \"Per-user, tenant and fleet quotas live in shared Postgres (quota.usage). Runs are reserved before work, but tokens and cost are charged only after each model call, so concurrent runs can overshoot: bound is roughly max_runs x per-run cap (150 x 0.40 USD per user per day vs 3.00 USD limit). Concurrent-run and charging-order attempts were not done in this batch, so no yes.\")\nE\ncat > work/b08.py <<'E'\nimport sys; sys.path.insert(0,\"work\")\nfrom drive import *\nN=\"k8s/networkpolicy.yaml\"\ncheck(\"B08.1\",\"yes\",N,\"name: default-deny-all\",\"Namespace hr-agent has a default-deny policy for ingress and egress; the agent and gateway then allow only named peers.\",\n counter=\"Searched for 0.0.0.0/0, toCIDR allows and wildcard peers: none in allow rules; only egressDeny CIDRs.\",\n rows=[row(\"default deny\",\"enforced\",N,\"policyTypes: [Ingress, Egress]\",\"all pods in hr-agent denied by default\"),\n       row(\"agent->DNS\",\"enforced\",N,\"- matchName: api.anthropic.com\",\"DNS answers limited to named hosts and cluster services\"),\n       row(\"agent->api.anthropic.com and sso\",\"enforced\",N,\"- matchName: sso.acme.example\",\"FQDN allow for the model API and SSO\"),\n       row(\"agent->gateway\",\"enforced\",N,\"- matchLabels: {app: hr-tool-gateway}\",\"named gateway peer on 8443\"),\n       row(\"agent-