{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChG2UGpFJnkaWprUtvyPU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed B06–B10 and saved the findings to `agent/brace-findings.json`. The batch validator (`--before-challenges`) reports it valid: 3 gaps, 1 likely_pass and 1 needs_evidence. I did not run challenges, falsification attempts or the topology map, and I added no other items.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| B06 Approval integrity | gap | Approvals are bound to instance, operation, target and argument hash, and consumed in one atomic UPDATE. The reviewer description (`src/approvals.py:31`) leaves out the `note` argument, which is approved and sent. B06.1 is `unknown` because the grants table has no scope column. |\n| B07 Execution budgets | needs_evidence | All six run limits and the per-user, tenant and fleet quotas exist. B07.2 and B07.4 are `unknown` because I skipped the boundary and concurrent-run traces. Concurrent runs can overshoot the quotas, roughly 150 runs × $0.40 against a $3 user limit. The SDK retry (`max_retries=1`) is not counted separately. |\n| B08 Environment isolation | likely_pass | The namespace is default-deny with named peers, metadata addresses are blocked, and there are no host mounts. It still needs a fresh challenge. |\n| B09 Egress allowlist | gap | `src/gateway_client.py:52` falls back to a direct route when the gateway is down. `k8s/networkpolicy.yaml` lets the agent reach `helpdesk-mcp` directly, so `create_ticket` can skip the gateway checks (B09.2). B09.3–B09.5 are `unknown`. |\n| B10 Pinned, verified image | gap | Images are digest-pinned and signature-checked against a pinned identity and issuer. `k8s/admission.yaml` has no rule denying images that match no `verifyImages` entry (B10.4), and the `platform/*` rule has no provenance check (B10.3). B10.5 is `unknown` because the Kyverno version is not pinned in the repo. |\n\nPre-scan hit H008 (`body[\"approval\"] = state.pending_approval`) is dismissed. That line copies server-built approval data into the response; the model never writes it.\n\nThe `unknown` answers on B06.1 and B09.3 are judgment calls where I chose not to record a `no`. I used `no` on B10.3 because the `platform/*` rule has no attestation block.\n\nThe scripts only run without `-I`, because they import their sibling modules. I ran them that way with the supplied interpreter. My helper scripts are in `work/`, outside `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":553,"cache_read_input_tokens":101883,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":553},"output_tokens":776,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59246f9b-6f28-4e6c-8986-ba3133bba698","uuid":"b0068fb6-c9a7-40e5-9297-2f53f1defb3e","timestamp":"2026-11-21T11:52:38.410Z","request_id":"req_011ChG2UGf4wzrGr6yJUS9AQ"}
